      {
        "id": "p9-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Why is it impossible to tell on how many days the maximum temperature was above $25^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$25^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$ lies within the $24.9$–$25.1^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$ class, so its frequency does not show how many values were above $25^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$.",
          "worked": "The $24.9$–$25.1^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$ class contains 4 days. The table does not separate these into temperatures of $24.9^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$, $25.0^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$ and $25.1^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$. Therefore, we cannot determine how many of those days were above $25^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$.",
